  "theorem_statement": "At the registered multiplier root, the saved carrier chart identifies exceptional point 0 by the relational predicate that its two endpoint connectors have equal ordered voltage pairs and neither carrier holonomy equals its open-path voltage product. This predicate survives all six global renamings of the nonidentity V4 elements. It does not define a native selector: in the fixed chart it matches only 8 of 120 transported rooted actions, and under the 32768 independent local a-gauge switches it selects point 0 in only 3584 gauges. A single a-switch at the root changes the selection from point 0 to point 1.",
